// Anomaly definitions for Helios Ascension (v0.5.0 PR-C).
//
// Drives the r2 anomaly confidence model: per-tick detection roll,
// confidence accumulation, retry-pressure ramp, activation /
// refutation. See `docs/design/SURVEY_REWORK.md` §12.
//
// Modding Guide:
// - Add a new row to `hardcoded` to ship with the binary; the
//   `id` must match an `AnomalyType::ron_id` variant.
// - Add a new row to `modder_anomalies` for modder-added types —
//   the loader turns each into an `AnomalyDef` at startup.
// - `detection_axes` lists the dimensions whose tier must meet
//   `detection_threshold` for the roll to fire.
// - `false_positive_rate` is the per-roll probability the system
//   ignores the candidate. Modders tune per anomaly in `[0.05, 0.30]`.
// - `activation_threshold` is the confidence required to promote
//   the anomaly to `Verified`. Retry-pressure reduces it.
// - `evidence_methods` lists the methods that count as "verification"
//   for this anomaly. `method_specificity` overrides the
//   default per-method weight for any of them.
// - `effect` is what the anomaly does on activation. `None` is
//   flavor-only; the others route through research/buildings/events.

(
    hardcoded: [
        // ── r1 terrestrial anomalies (9 from PR-A) ────────────────
        (
            id: "water_ice_deposit",
            display_name: "Water Ice Deposit",
            description: "Significant subsurface water-ice deposit. Routes to a water-extraction building.",
